%S A399564 10,46,220,1054,5050,24196,115930,555454,2661340,12751246,61094890,
%T A399564 292723204,1402521130,6719882446,32196891100,154264573054,
%U A399564 739125974170,3541365297796,16967700514810,81297137276254,389517985866460,1866292792056046,8941945974413770,42843437080012804
%N A399564 Number of perfect matchings of the 3 X 2n grid graph embedded on the Klein bottle.
%C A399564 The cycle is in the vertical direction and the twist in the horizontal direction.
%C A399564 The characteristic polynomial of the order-2 recurrence is x^2 - 5*x + 1, with dominant root (5 + sqrt(21))/2 ~ 4.791.
%H A399564 Jean Lauro Muller, <a href="/A399564/a399564.py.txt">Python program</a>
%H A399564 <a href="/index/Rec#order_02">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (5,-1).
%F A399564 a(n) = 5*a(n-1) - a(n-2) for n >= 3, with a(1) = 10, a(2) = 46.
%F A399564 G.f.: 2*x*(5 - 2*x)/(1 - 5*x + x^2).
%F A399564 E.g.f.: 4*(exp(5*x/2)*cosh(sqrt(21)*x/2) - 1). - _Stefano Spezia_, Sep 05 2026
%e A399564 For n=1, the 3 X 2 Klein bottle grid has a(1) = 10 perfect matchings.
%e A399564 For n=2, the 3 X 4 grid has a(2) = 46 perfect matchings.
%e A399564 For n=3, the 3 X 6 grid has a(3) = 220 perfect matchings.
%t A399564 LinearRecurrence[{5, -1}, {10, 46}, 25]
%o A399564 (Python)
%o A399564 def A_list(N):
%o A399564     seq = [10, 46]
%o A399564     for n in range(3, N + 1):
%o A399564         seq.append(5*seq[-1] - seq[-2])
%o A399564     return seq[:N]
%Y A399564 Cf. A398567 (Klein bottle 2n X 3), A398672 (Klein bottle 4 X 2n), A397309 (Klein bottle 5 X 2n), A399275 (Klein bottle 6 X 2n), A399311 (Klein bottle 7 X 2n).
%K A399564 nonn,easy,new
%O A399564 1,1
%A A399564 _Jean Lauro Muller_, Sep 03 2026
